#!/usr/bin/env python3
# =====================================================================
# rvlinux  -  Linux on the boot platform, from source (Step 53)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
#   tools/rvlinux all [--fast]     fetch + build + run   (make linux)
#   tools/rvlinux fetch            pinned sources into third_party/
#   tools/rvlinux build            musl, busybox, initramfs, kernel -> build/linux/
#   tools/rvlinux run [--fast]     boot it on soc_boot (DDR), type at the shell, check
#
# fetch   clones Linux, busybox and musl at pinned tags and checks each
#         commit hash, so a mirror cannot hand over anything else.
# build   musl as an rv32ima ilp32 (soft-float) libc; busybox, static,
#         from sw/linux/busybox.config; an initramfs of busybox, /init and
#         matest; the kernel from tinyconfig + sw/linux/kernel.config.
# run     wraps the kernel's Image as a boot image (tools/rvboot's format)
#         for 0x80400000 (RAM + 4 MiB: Sv32 wants the kernel 4 MiB
#         aligned), boots soc_boot with 64 MiB of DDR under tb/boot_tb.v,
#         and at each "rvfs# " prompt types the next command. Then checks
#         the transcript: the boot, each command's output, a clean power-off.
#         The whole kernel goes over the simulated serial line, 160 clocks
#         a byte: ~420M cycles before Linux runs, ~15 minutes in all.
#         --fast: the bench preloads the kernel into the DDR model and the
#         ROM receives only its first 4 KiB (~5 minutes). Everything after
#         the ROM is the same.
#         --board (Step 54; implies --fast): the board's configuration
#         instead -- the board ROM, 115200 baud from 50 MHz, and the 64 MiB
#         over a 64-bit S_AXI_HP-shaped port at DDR 0x1000_0000.
#         --frommem (Step 56): the whole image preloaded at 0x8300_0000, where
#         the PS leaves it from flash; the ROM boots it with nothing sent.
#
# For the Mitra-7010 board (Step 54):
#   tools/rvlinux board-image      build/linux/linux-board.rvbi (bootargs at 115200)
#   tools/rvlinux oz-export OZ     write projects/riscv_linux into an OpenZynq
#                                  checkout: rtl/fpga_top_linux.v on the PS7 with
#                                  S_AXI_HP0, its pins, the PS program, a testbench,
#                                  boot.bif and fw/boot.rvbi for BOOT.BIN (Step 56)
#   tools/rvlinux oz-sim OZ        that top with the checkout's own ps7_gp0, a PS7
#                                  model and a DDR model, under verilator: the ROM,
#                                  a bad image, libc_demo from DDR (~1 minute)
#
# Requires: git, make, flex, bison, bc, rsync; riscv64-linux-gnu-gcc (the
# kernel and musl); riscv64-unknown-elf-gcc (its rv32im/ilp32 libgcc, which
# the Linux toolchain lacks); verilator 5.x; and build/boot/rom.hex (make
# boot-sw) -- or build/boot/linux-board/rom.hex (make boot-board) for the board.
# Sources: ~2 GB, build: ~0.5 GB.
# =====================================================================
